title: [+ year +] <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> Conference
subtitle: The fate of Stegerwald's reforms is decided
view-if: year = 1929 and month >= 12 and z_leader = "Stegerwald"
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

= Center Party Conference

Stegerwald's actions have solidified the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> as an interconfessional party, but he has made plenty of enemies in doing so. Former chancellor Joseph Wirth and his allies in the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span> are opposing his leadership.

Jakob Kaiser, a rising star on the left, who supports a united Christian union, but opposes Stegerwald's right-wind policies is best placed to challenge him.

- @z_stegerwald: The Center Party elects Adam Stegerwald as the party chair.
- @z_kaiser: The Center Party elects Jakob Kaiser as the party chair.

@z_stegerwald
on-arrival: z_leader = "Stegerwald"; z_ideology = "Right";
face-image: img/portraits/StegerwaldAdam.jpg

Stegerwald will continue to evolve the <span style="color: #000000;">Center Party</span> into a <span style="color: #000000;">Christian</span>, <span style="color: #586593;">democratic</span>, <span style="color: #000000;">German</span>, and <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> party. [? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": Now taking the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>'s place on the German right. ?]

[? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": There are already rumors of a merger with <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>'s place on the German right. ?]

@z_joos
unavailable-subtitle: Joos doesn't have enough support.
on-arrival: z_leader = "Joos"; z_ideology = "Left"; z_relation -= 2 if dvp_ideology = "Right"; workers_z += 3, catholics_z -= 3
choose-if: not prussia_leader = "Stegerwald" and pro_republic >= 65
face-image: img/portraits/JoosJoseph.jpg

Joseph Joos has been selected as the chairman of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span>. He has long been a friend of the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>, and will be more inclined to collaborate with them compared to Kaas. He also increases the appeal of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> to the working class.

@z_stegerwald
unavailable-subtitle: Stegerwald lacks the influence necessary to have a real chance.
choose-if: prussia_leader = "Stegerwald"
on-arrival: z_leader = "Stegerwald"; z_ideology = "Right"; new_middle_z -= 5; old_middle_z -= 3; catholics_z -= 5; workers_z += 5
face-image: img/portraits/StegerwaldAdam.jpg

Adam Stegerwald has been elected as the chairman of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span>. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Marx, despite his trade union background, and will preside over a <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> less inclined to compromise with the left. He views the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> as a prototype for a Christian, democratic, German, and social party, and aims to transform it according to the principles laid out in his proposed "Essen program" eight years prior.
